{
  "schema_version": "1.9.2",
  "id": "USN-9202-1",
  "summary": "krb5 vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that the Kerberos KDC incorrectly handled certain ASN.1\nencodings in requests. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to\ncause the KDC to crash, resulting in a denial of service.\n(CVE-2026-107364)\n\nIt was discovered that the Kerberos KDC incorrectly handled malformed\nclient names in PAC data during S4U2Proxy requests. A remote attacker\ncontrolling a trusted cross-realm KDC could possibly use this issue to\ncause the KDC to crash, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only\naffected Ubuntu 24.04 LTS and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-107708)\n\nIt was discovered that Kerberos incorrectly handled certain KRB-CRED\nmessages. A remote authenticated attacker could possibly use this issue to\ncause services that accept forwarded credentials to crash, resulting in a\ndenial of service. (CVE-2026-107778)\n\nIt was discovered that the Kerberos password change service did not\nenforce the lockdown_keys principal attribute. An authenticated attacker\nwith administrative privileges could possibly use this issue to bypass\nsecurity restrictions and change the keys of a protected principal.\n(CVE-2026-107884)\n\nIt was discovered that Kerberos incorrectly handled PAC server checksum\nverification. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to bypass\nsecurity restrictions. This issue only affected Ubuntu 26.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-111423)\n\nIt was discovered that the Kerberos GSS-RPC client did not properly free\nmemory when handling certain replies. A remote attacker could possibly use\nthis issue to cause Kerberos client programs to consume excessive memory,\nleading to a denial of service. (CVE-2026-112314)\n\nIt was discovered that the Kerberos GSS-RPC library did not properly free\nmemory under certain circumstances. A remote attacker could possibly use\nthese issues to cause the Kerberos administration server to consume\nexcessive memory, leading to a denial of service. (CVE-2026-112315,\nCVE-2026-112316, CVE-2026-112320, CVE-2026-112321)\n\nIt was discovered that Kerberos did not properly free decrypted key\nmaterial when a post-decryption check failed. A remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause the Kerberos KDC or administration server\nto consume excessive memory, leading to a denial of service.\n(CVE-2026-112317)\n\nIt was discovered that the Kerberos administration server did not properly\nhandle empty policy names. An authenticated attacker could possibly use\nthis issue to cause the Kerberos administration server to crash, resulting\nin a denial of service. (CVE-2026-112318)\n\nIt was discovered that the Kerberos GSS-RPC library did not enforce size\nlimits when decoding data. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto cause the Kerberos administration server to consume excessive\nresources, leading to a denial of service. (CVE-2026-112319)\n\nIt was discovered that the legacy AUTH_GSSAPI authentication flavor in the\nKerberos administration server lacked protections against resource\nexhaustion. A remote attacker could possibly use these issues to cause the\nKerberos administration server to consume excessive resources, leading to\na denial of service. This update disables AUTH_GSSAPI in the Kerberos\nadministration server by default. It can be re-enabled by setting the\nGSSRPC_ALLOW_AUTH_GSSAPI environment variable for kadmind.\n(CVE-2026-112322, CVE-2026-112323)\n\nIt was discovered that Kerberos did not properly verify RPCSEC_GSS call\narguments. An attacker in a machine-in-the-middle position could possibly\nuse this issue to alter the arguments sent by a legitimate client to RPC\nservices, or cause return values to be sent in plain text.\n(CVE-2026-118380)\n\nIt was discovered that Kerberos inefficiently decoded long ASN.1\nsequences. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\nKerberos to consume excessive CPU resources, leading to a denial of\nservice. (CVE-2026-119079)\n\nAlejandro Pacheco discovered that Kerberos did not reject unkeyed\nchecksums in CAMMAC verifiers. An authenticated attacker could possibly\nuse this issue to bypass authentication indicator requirements.\n(CVE-2026-71199)\n\nErin Liman discovered that the Kerberos PKINIT module incorrectly handled\ncertain CMS messages. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to\ncause the KDC to crash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-71200)",
